                stops.append(floor)
            if direction == 1 and floor == top_floor:
                break
            if direction == -1 and floor == 1:
                break
        return stops

The range walks the floors from the start in the given direction, with floor 1 always included as the endpoint in a downward sweep, and the top floor in the upward direction. In the downward case, the range is written as range(start, top + 1, -1), so the final value top + 1 means the last floor examined is top. The start floor itself is visited first, so if it appears in requests it is included; when it does not, the empty early list is shared with the start at floor 1.

