A 90-degree rotation of an n x m grid moves row i of column j to row j of column n-1-i. Rotating twice is 180 degrees, rotating three times is 270 degrees, and rotating the fourth time returns to the original. The helper function below rotates a grid by a given number of turns and returns one.

    def rotate(grid, turns):
        n, m = len(grid), len(grid[0])
        result = [[0 for _ in range(n)] for _ in range(m)]
        for i in range(n):
            for j in range(m):
                result[(j + turns) % n][n - 1 - i] = grid[i][j]
        return result

