I represent the queue as a deque, which makes removing from the left fast. For an arrival, I append the person's ID to the end. For a service call, I pop the first item up to capacity times. Python's slice assignment helps here: popping from the front capacity times is the same as shortening the deque to length at most capacity. Popping too many times leaves capacity items, and popping out of range has no effect, which covers the case where the queue is plentiful or empty.

