A clean implementation would keep a queue and iterate over the events while building it. A single serve event can delete the first min(len(queue), capacity) people. For example, the first two asserts send people 1 and 2 in order, followed by serve with capacities 1 and 5. The first serve clears only 1, leaving 2; the second clears both. Nothing in those asserts exercises arriving after serving, so I focused on arrival orders and capacities the asserts do not use.

The relevant part of the full solution is:

